[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 079]   Warsaw, CODE, and MW08 share fitting machinery, so the transit
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 079]   replication is independent in sample rather than in method.  MPC's
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 079]   CometEls is a fourth, separately maintained fit record.  For every
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 079]   comet appearing in both CometEls and CODE osculating (or Warsaw
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 079]   osculating), the periapsis-direction difference between the two
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 079]   fitters is the direct, per-object lineage noise floor.  If the in-cap
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 079]   orig->fut anomaly (~0.14 deg) sits far above that floor, and the floor
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 079]   itself is cap-symmetric, a shared fitter convention cannot be the
[2026-09-21 14:51:27 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 079]   explanation.
